ID":"QID39"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID40","SecondaryAttribute":"Which researcher is more likely to get a job?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Which researcher is more likely to get a job?","DataExportTag":"minget","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Which researcher is more likely to get a job?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"reported researcher (K)"},"2":{"Display":"neither reported (K) nor reporting researcher (S)"},"3":{"Display":"reporting researcher (S)"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID40"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID41","SecondaryAttribute":"Scenario Researcher H conducted a study and found an interesting result. After publication, Resea...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">Scenario<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n<br>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">Researcher H conducted a study and found an interesting result. After publication, Researcher H\u2019s data and materials were made available to the public. While looking through the open data, it was discovered that Researcher H had played around with excluding certain data points until they achieved a significant result to be able to publish.<br>\n<br>\nAfter examining the dataset, Researcher F writes a blog post presenting evidence on how Researcher H manipulated their data to achieve statistically significant results. Researcher F emphasizes that this practice misleads the scientific community and undermines the credibility of science.&nbsp;<\/span><\/span>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Scenario Researcher H conducted a study and found an interesting result. After publication, Resea...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">Scenario 1<\/span><\/span><\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">Researcher K conducted a study and found an interesting result. Researcher K&rsquo;s project paper was published and made available to the public. Researcher K submitted the findings to a journal for publication, but the abstract implied the study had much broader implications than the study truly did.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nResearcher S after reading the abstract, writes a blog post highlighting how Researcher K&rsquo;s misrepresentations can mislead readers about the scope and findings of the research. Researcher S emphasizes the importance of crafting precise titles and abstracts to ensure that research is accurately represented and understood, warning that misleading summaries can undermine the credibility of science.<\/span><\/span>","DataExportTag":"scen 2","QuestionID":"QID41"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID42","SecondaryAttribute":"The following questions are specifically about RESEARCHER H. \u00a0As a reminder: Researcher H conduct..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><u><strong>The following questions are specifically about RESEARCHER H.<\/strong><\/u><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">&nbsp;As a reminder:<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"background-color:#ffccff;\">Researcher H conducted a study and found an interesting result. After publication, Researcher H&rsquo;s data and materials were made available to the public. While looking through the open data, it was discovered that Researcher H had played around with excluding certain data points until they achieved a significant result to be able to publish.<\/span><br \/>\n<br \/>\nAfter examining the dataset, Researcher F writes a blog post presenting evidence on how Researcher H manipulated their data to achieve statistically significant results. Researcher F emphasizes that this practice misleads the scientific community and undermines the credibility of science.&nbsp;<\/span><\/span>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"The following questions are specifically about RESEARCHER H. \u00a0As a reminder: Researcher H conduct...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><u><strong>The following questions are specifically about RESEARCHER K.<\/strong><\/u><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">&nbsp;As a reminder:<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"background-color:#ffff99;\">Researcher K conducted a study and found an interesting result. Researcher K&rsquo;s project paper was published and made available to the public. Researcher K submitted the findings to a journal for publication, but the abstract implied the study had much broader implications than the study truly did.&nbsp;<\/span><br \/>\n<br \/>\nResearcher S after reading the abstract, writes a blog post highlighting how Researcher K&rsquo;s misrepresentations can mislead readers about the scope and findings of the research. Researcher S emphasizes the importance of crafting precise titles and abstracts to ensure that research is accurately represented and understood, warning that misleading summaries can undermine the credibility of science.<\/span><\/span>","DataExportTag":"hremind","QuestionID":"QID42"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID43","SecondaryAttribute":"How honest or dishonest is Researcher H?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How honest or dishonest is <b>Researcher H<\/b>?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"How honest or dishonest is Researcher H?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1 = very dishonest"},"2":{"Display":"2 = somewhat dishonest"},"3":{"Display":"3 = neither honest nor dishonest"},"4":{"Display":"4 = somewhat honest"},"5":{"Display":"5 = very honest"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"How honest or dishonest is <b>Researcher K<\/b> ?","DataExportTag":"Hhon","QuestionID":"QID43"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID44","SecondaryAttribute":"How sincere or insincere is Researcher H\u00a0?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How sincere or insincere is <b>Researcher H<\/b>&nbsp;?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"How sincere or insincere is Researcher H\u00a0?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1 = very insincere"},"2":{"Display":"2 = somewhat insincere"},"3":{"Display":"3 = neither sincere nor insincere"},"4":{"Display":"4 = somewhat sincere"},"5":{"Display":"5 = very sincere"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"How sincere or insincere is <b>Researcher K<\/b> ?","DataExportTag":"Hsin","QuestionID":"QID44"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID45","SecondaryAttribute":"How ethical or unethical is Researcher H?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How ethical or unethical is <b>Researcher H<\/b>?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"How ethical or unethical is Researcher H?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1 = very unethical"},"2":{"Display":"2 = somewhat unethical"},"3":{"Display":"3 = neither ethical nor unethical"},"4":{"Display":"4 = somewhat ethical"},"5":{"Display":"5 = very ethical"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"How ethical or unethical is <b>Researcher K<\/b> ?","DataExportTag":"Seth","QuestionID":"QID45"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID46","SecondaryAttribute":"How likeable or unlikeable is Researcher H\u00a0?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How likeable or unlikeable is <b>Researcher H<\/b>&nbsp;?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"How likeable or unlikeable is Researcher H\u00a0?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1 = very unlikeable"},"2":{"Display":"2 = somewhat unlikeable"},"3":{"Display":"3 = neither likeable nor unlikeable"},"4":{"Display":"4 = somewhat likeable"},"5":{"Display":"5 = very likeable"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"How likeable or unlikeable is <b>Researcher K<\/b> ?","DataExportTag":"Hlike","QuestionID":"QID46"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID47","SecondaryAttribute":"How approachable or unapproachable is Researcher H\u00a0?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How approachable or unapproachable is <b>Researcher H<\/b>&nbsp;?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"How approachable or unapproachable is Researcher H\u00a0?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1 = very unapproachable"},"2":{"Display":"2 = somewhat unapproachable"},"3":{"Display":"3 = neither approachable nor unapproachable"},"4":{"Display":"4 = somewhat approachable"},"5":{"Display":"5 = very approachable"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"How approachable or unapproachable is <b>Researcher K<\/b> ?","DataExportTag":"Happ","QuestionID":"QID47"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID48","SecondaryAttribute":"Based on what you know about the actions of Researcher H, how confident are you that their report...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Based on what you know about the actions of Researcher H, how confident are you that their reported findings are true?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Based on what you know about the actions of Researcher H, how confident are you that their report...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1 = very confident the findings are false"},"2":{"Display":"2 = somewhat confident the findings are false"},"3":{"Display":"3 = could go either way"},"4":{"Display":"4 = somewhat confident the findings are true"},"5":{"Display":"5 = very confident the findings are true"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Based on what you know about the actions of Researcher K, how confident are you that their reported findings are true?","DataExportTag":"Hcon","QuestionID":"QID48"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID49","SecondaryAttribute":"The following questions are specifically about RESEARCHER F. \u00a0As a reminder: Researcher H conduct..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><u><strong>The following questions are specifically about RESEARCHER F.<\/strong><\/u><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">&nbsp;As a reminder:<br \/>\n<br \/>\nResearcher H conducted a study and found an interesting result. After publication, Researcher H&rsquo;s data and materials were made available to the public. While looking through the open data, it was discovered that Researcher H had played around with excluding certain data points until they achieved a significant result to be able to publish.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"background-color:#99ff99;\">After examining the dataset, Researcher F writes a blog post presenting evidence on how Researcher H manipulated their data to achieve statistically significant results. Researcher F emphasizes that this practice misleads the scientific community and undermines the credibility of science.&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><\/span>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"The following questions are specifically about RESEARCHER F. \u00a0As a reminder: Researcher H conduct...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:19px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><u><strong>The following questions are specifically about RESEARCHER S.<\/strong><\/u><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">&nbsp;As a reminder:<br \/>\n<br \/>\nResearcher K conducted a study and found an interesting result. Researcher K&rsquo;s project paper was published and made available to the public. Researcher K submitted the findings to a journal for publication, but the abstract implied the study had much broader implications than the study truly did.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"background-color:#99ffff;\">Researcher S after reading the abstract, writes a blog post highlighting how Researcher K&rsquo;s misrepresentations can mislead readers about the scope and findings of the research. Researcher S emphasizes the importance of crafting precise titles and abstracts to ensure that research is accurately represented and understood, warning that misleading summaries can undermine the credibility of science.<\/span><\/span><\/span>","DataExportTag":"Fremind","QuestionID":"QID49"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID5","SecondaryAttribute":"Informed Consent Please read this informed consent carefully before you decide to participate in...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><u><strong>Informed Consent<\/strong><\/u><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><em>Please read this informed consent carefully before you decide to participate in the study. <\/em><\/span><\/span><\/div>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><strong>Consent Form Key Information:<\/strong><\/span><\/span>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">You will participate in a thirty-minute study about perceptions of researchers <\/span><\/span><\/li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">No information collected will connect your identity to your responses <\/span><\/span><br \/>\n\t&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"> <span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"> <strong>Purpose of the research study:<\/strong><br \/>\nWe are interested in how prior exposure to information relates to how people evaluate researchers. In this study, you will be asked to read scenarios about researchers and provide your perceptions of those researchers.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>What you will do in the study:<\/strong><br \/>\nIf you consent to participate in this study, you will take a survey online with a desktop, laptop, or other sufficiently powerful mobile device. You will be asked a series of questions related to the research scenarios. At the end of the survey, you will be provided with a Debriefing Statement with more information regarding the study and research goals. The goals of the study will be withheld from participants until completion of the survey to avoid interference with study aims. The entire survey should take less than thirty minutes to complete.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>Time required:<\/strong><br \/>\nThe survey will require about thirty minutes of your time.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>Risks:<\/strong><br \/>\nThe risks of participating in this study are expected to be minimal. The effects are likely to be transient and not expected to be greater than those experienced in daily life. You may risk a loss of confidentiality if you choose to email researchers to ask for the results of the study. Researchers will immediately delete such emails after responding to them. There is a potential risk of loss of confidentiality in all email, downloading, and internet transactions.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>Benefits:<\/strong><br \/>\nThere are no direct benefits of your participation in this research study. The findings may help researchers better understand how repeated exposure to information relates to how people judge researchers. Additionally, this study provides first hand experience in the research process.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>Confidentiality:<\/strong><br \/>\nData will be accessible to everyone, but will never be paired with measures that may be identifying or harmful to you as a participant. All data will be reported at the group level and will be presented as individual responses. There may be a risk of a loss of confidentiality if you choose to email the researchers to ask for the results of the study. If emailed, then the researchers will immediately delete such emails after responding to them. There is an ever-present risk of loss of confidentiality in all email, downloading, and internet transactions. Study links will be set to not track or collect any IP addresses from participants in the study. The information that you give in the study will be handled confidentially. Your name and other information that could be used to identify you will not be collected or linked to the data.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>Voluntary participation:<\/strong><br \/>\nYour participation in the study is completely voluntary. ####Right to withdraw from the study: You have the right to withdraw from the study at any time without penalty.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>How to withdraw from the study:<\/strong><br \/>\nIf you want to withdraw from the study and have not yet completed the survey, you may simply stop taking the survey. If you have completed the study, there will be an option to select that you would not like your data to be included in any analysis and have it withdrawn\/deleted. Beyond this point, however, there will be no additional opportunities to withdraw; after the survey is submitted and data is collected, there is no way to attribute data to any particular participant to have it deleted. There is no penalty for withdrawing. You will still receive full credit for the study. If you would like to withdraw after your materials have been submitted, please contact Savannah Lewis.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<strong>Compensation\/Reimbursement:<\/strong><br \/>\nYou will receive no payment for participating in the study. Students will receive .5 class participation credit needed for introductory psychology courses. Using data beyond this study: In line with open-science practices, the researcher would like to make the information collected in this study available to other researchers after the study is completed. Your information will be stored, used, and shared for future research studies, including but not limited to meta-analyses and secondary data analyses. Researchers of future studies will not ask your permission for each new study. However, the information you provide will be combined with the information provided by others to create a large data set. Your name and other information that could potentially identify you will not be connected to the information shared with other researchers, nor will they attempt to identify you. If you have questions about the study or need to report a study related issue please contact:<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<em>Name of Principal Investigator:<\/em> Savannah Lewis<br \/>\n<em>Title:<\/em> Graduate student<br \/>\n<em>Department Name: <\/em>Psychology<br \/>\n<em>Telephone:<\/em> 740-503-3674<br \/>\n<em>Email address<\/em>: slewis20@crimson.ua.edu<br \/>\n<br \/>\nThis research has been reviewed and approved by an Institutional Review Board (&ldquo;IRB&rdquo;). If you have questions, concerns, or complaints, or think the research has hurt you, you may email the Office for Research Compliance at rscompliance@ua.edu or call (205) 348-8641 and ask about: <\/span><\/span>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">Your questions, concerns, or complaints are not being answered by the research team.<\/span><\/span><\/li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">You cannot reach the research team. <\/span><\/span><\/li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">You want to talk to someone besides the research team. <\/span><\/span><\/li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">You have questions about your rights as a research subject. <\/span><\/span><\/li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\">You want to get information or provide input about this research. <\/span><\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<br \/>\n<span style=\"font-size:16px;\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;\"><strong>Agreement:<\/strong><br \/>\nIf you agree with the following statement, you may continue with the study:<br \/>\n<br \/>\nThe purpose and the nature of this research have been sufficiently explained and I agree to participate in this study. I understand that I am free to withdraw at any time without incurring any penalty.<\/span><\/span>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Consent form\u00a0","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Informed Consent Please read this informed consent carefully before you decide to participate in...","Choices":{"3":{"Display":"Yes, I consent"},"4":{"Display":"No, I will leave the survey now"}},"ChoiceOrder":["3","4"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID5","Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"ConsistentScaleReversal":false,"EvenPresentation":false,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"None"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID50","SecondaryAttribute":"How honest or dishonest is Researcher F\u00a0?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How honest or dishonest is <b>Researcher F<\/b>&nbsp;?","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"How honest or dishonest is Researcher F\u00a0?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"1 = very dishonest"},"2":{"Display":"2 = somewhat dishonest"},"3":{"Display":"3 = neither honest nor dishonest"},"4":{"Display":"4 = somewhat honest"},"5":{"Display":"5 = very honest"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"How honest or dishonest is <b>Researcher S<\/b> ?","DataExportTag":"Fhin","QuestionID":"QID50"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_d0XMwEApRDPv1mC","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID51","SecondaryAttribute":"How sincere or insincere is Researcher F\u00a0?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How sincere or insince